comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T07:32:05.563Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus of 3242 items including 2923 closed items and request-specific keyword search reviewed. No matching owner for this GitHub report. Reuse the existing parent capability and preserve closed recovery/configuration lineage."
  "2026-11-09T07:48:19.904Z","harness:codex","Negative-control evidence: new regression assertions ran against unchanged production source before the fix. The focused run failed exactly the settings-path, leading-slash source, matcher-index and strict-close-headline assertions: 4 failures and176 existing passes. Production repair preserves existing validators and sensitive input redaction."
  "2026-11-09T08:30:38.246Z","harness:codex","Completeness review extended the same descriptor-owned configuration surface to the context scalar leaves previously available only through grouped context flags: default depth, activity limit, staleness threshold and the eight existing section toggles. The shared descriptor validators enforce the canonical depth domain, positive safe integers and booleans; real CLI tests check persisted values and byte preservation on invalid depth, zero and unsafe-integer assignments. Existing grouped flags remain supported and help now distinguishes group and leaf writes."
  "2026-11-09T09:53:13.176Z","harness:codex","PR #1696 review remediation: unknown-key inspections retain requested project/global scope; telemetry typo suggestions explicitly identify global-only consent. Dotted context integer leaves reuse the existing complete positive-decimal validator, refusing scientific/hex notation before writes; --default-depth help now includes full. Focused regression and real parser persistence checks are included with the review batch."
  "2026-11-09T10:22:43.102Z","harness:codex","The new direct SDK round-trip regression caught a real persistence mismatch: context.default_depth=full was accepted by the SDK but the settings read validator admitted only brief/standard/deep and returned fallback settings on the next get. The same public CONTEXT_DEPTH_VALUES domain must govern settings reads. This is fixed under the existing configuration owner, with the failing SDK round-trip retained as the negative control."
  "2026-11-09T10:24:42.667Z","harness:codex","Direct SDK regression strengthened the existing nested-leaf owner with context depth/activity/staleness/section round-trips and exact settings-byte preservation for non-decimal/zero refusals. It failed before the full-depth read-validator fix (full resolved as brief), then passed with shared CONTEXT_DEPTH_VALUES. The combined settings/guidance/parser cohort passes 171 tests. Only this configuration owner and pm-gh1693 were reclaimed for these edits."
  "2026-11-09T11:41:56.128Z","harness:codex","Review batch regression control: four intended failures (missing context toggles, incomplete declared recovery aliases, and scientific-number acceptance by profile lint) preceded the shared descriptor fix. All 232 tests across eight files then passed under source instrumentation. Decimal-only context validation is declared internally and reused by profile lint/planning plus grouped/dotted setters; generic integer knobs preserve existing Number syntax. Inventory uses existing summary/min/max fields, avoiding an unnecessary public result-shape extension flagged by the SDK signature gate."
  "2026-11-09T11:55:37.095Z","harness:codex","Final public SDK surface verification reports zero classified changes after keeping numeric-format discovery in the existing metadata fields. Configuration/profile and release/guidance cohorts pass 232 tests; source instrumentation covers the changed strict-integer parser, key recovery and grouped-context parser branches. The optional metadata-only inventory enhancement is separately tracked open/unclaimed in pm-8txeqe."
  "2026-11-09T12:51:18.111Z","harness:codex","Second full-review repair: grouped context integer refusals name the decimal-digits-only grammar. Both grouped numeric options reject scientific notation with that actionable message and preserve settings bytes; project allowed-values regression now excludes both telemetry-tracking and telemetry.enabled. The pre-fix grouped grammar test failed as intended; all 168 focused tests pass."
  "2026-11-09T14:00:02.690Z","harness:codex",Grouped context integer errors now state the shared maximum safe integer as well as decimal-digit syntax. Both grouped numeric options reject overflow with that bound and preserve the settings bytes. The overflow message assertions failed before the wording repair and pass afterward.
  "2026-11-09T15:28:13.110Z","harness:codex","Strict decimal grammar now runs before Number conversion. Dotted invalid values such as 10days and fractions report decimal syntax and actual declared bounds, including finite-overflow strings; generic numeric settings retain their previous Number syntax. The descriptor unit and real SDK settings-byte assertions fail before and pass after the change. Grouped flag guidance still exposes its positive safe-integer domain. The separate requested required.supported_keys field is intentionally mapped to governed recovery.allowed_values to preserve the published required string contract."
  "2026-11-09T15:59:08.393Z","harness:codex",Final source inspection found that new recovery commands retain project/global scope but omit GlobalOptions tracker/extension selection. Reuse this canonical working-inventory owner. Add a two-tracker replay with an ambient-tracker negative control and render coordinates through the existing SDK command-scope and command-line primitives; do not add a separate path parser or duplicate PM item.
  "2026-11-09T16:09:03.502Z","harness:codex","The two-tracker SDK replay exposed a second concrete defect in the original inventory suggestion: config list is not a universal read-output surface, so --output-budget unbounded makes the emitted command refuse before execution. Remove that unsupported flag; config list --json already returns its complete typed inventory. Preserve selected --pm-path and --no-extensions using the existing SDK scope primitive. The real CLI replay must read selected tracker value 11 and, only after removing its selector, ambient value 22."
  "2026-11-09T16:11:29.744Z","harness:codex","Final scoped recovery evidence: both linked test commands pass, including the real shell replay against two isolated trackers (selected activity_limit 11, ambient negative-control 22) and preserved extension isolation. The initial missing-selector control failed as expected; executing the repaired command also caught and removed unsupported universal --output-budget from config list. SDK surface check reports zero classified changes; contracts/catalog and source/package/example typechecks pass. This corrects earlier evidence wording that described an unbounded flag: completeness comes from the native config JSON inventory, without a universal-output flag."
  "2026-11-09T16:13:19.137Z","harness:codex","Hosted shard-4 repair: the independent complete-inventory fixture now explicitly enumerates the thirteen supported context aliases and verifies their paths, preserving exact key/count assertions instead of weakening them or deriving expectations from production descriptors. All three linked commands pass after this repair. The source-instrumented review cohort passes 356 tests across thirteen files; whole-repository hosted exact-100% coverage remains mandatory, with no threshold or denominator change."
  "2026-11-09T16:30:55.225Z","harness:codex","DeepScan exact-head report for 66885b171: NULL_POINTER at config-positional-cli.integration.spec.ts:65, defect 240635101. GitHub exposes only the count; Chrome Computer Use host is unavailable. Read-only public provider API confirms the uninitialized refusal access. Replace non-null assertions with optional access and a real runtime guard; retain the real selected-tracker and negative-control replay. No production behavior or analyzer settings change."
  "2026-11-09T19:13:09.183Z","harness:codex","Review typing repair: the runtime-preserved recently_created and unparented context section booleans now appear as optional fields in ParsedSettings. A consumer typetest reproduced two TS2339 failures before repair and compiles after repair without casts. The existing validator round-trip asserts both true and false values. All four linked owner commands and the 433-test instrumented cohort pass. Full typecheck, ESLint and generated contracts/catalog checks pass; SDK surface classification remains zero changes because this parsed internal shape is outside the published SDK export surface."
  "2026-11-09T19:55:39.696Z","harness:codex","Documented string-choice and case normalization, opt-in finite decimal parsing, alias discovery and scoped SDK recovery, and key requirements by configuration action. These comments explain the shared configuration contract rather than changing its behavior. This addresses the verified review docstring warning: nine touched helpers lacked JSDoc. Build, repository docstring quality, ESLint, SDK surface and contracts/catalog checks pass. Independent before/after TypeScript emission is byte-identical with comments removed across all five changed source files. The prior 433-test instrumented runtime cohort remains applicable; no runtime assertions are repeated for this documentation-only change. The proposed required.supported_keys object conflicts with the governed string required field; the complete scoped SDK domain already uses recovery.allowed_values. The combined release/maintenance scope follows the explicit multi-item delivery request and linked PM owners."
  "2026-11-09T21:23:02.674Z","harness:codex","A zero grouped context value reproduced the missing lower-bound explanation before repair. Grouped integer refusals now reuse the shared descriptor parser error, retaining its precise grammar and minimum/maximum reason. The existing regression checks zero for both context knobs and confirms settings remain unchanged. The typed option union maps only to declared shared-registry entries; the internal non-null lookup expresses that invariant. No defensive runtime branch or production test seam was added. Typo ranking remains bounded on the refusal path and the complete machine domain is retained as required. Final source verification reports 436 tests passing across 17 instrumented files, all seven linked command entries across the three owners, full typechecks, ESLint, contracts/catalog, zero classified SDK surface changes, and all nine packed consumers. Full-source coverage correctly refuses the selected cohort denominator; hosted whole-repository coverage and current-head admission remain required. No coverage, performance or diagnostic budget is relaxed."
  "2026-11-10T00:10:34.611Z","harness:codex","Completed full review 6c3eece8b found no new functional defect. Its additional unverified import-placement note was verified against the file: readFile/path imports followed describe. Consolidated all imports at the module top without changing assertions or production code. Existing four real CLI integration tests and ESLint pass. Preserve the requested combined SDK/release cohort rather than applying the unrelated scope-splitting suggestion; all affected work has canonical PM ownership."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T15:15:30.252Z","harness:codex","Contract decision for the proposed required.supported_keys path: the published SDK/CLI error envelope declares required as a remediation string shared by all commands. Preserve that governed shape and expose the complete scoped key domain through the existing recovery.allowed_values primitive rather than creating a command-specific object or duplicate domain. The scoped unbounded inventory command and complete SDK error context provide retrieval when CLI diagnostic budgeting binds. This is an explicit compatibility decision rather than a claim that the proposed field was added."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T10:03:47.802Z","harness:codex","Settings paths must resolve through the existing SDK validators and scope rules rather than becoming a parallel write path. Test refusal preservation and consent scope with real settings bytes, including typo suggestions and non-decimal integers."
  "2026-11-09T10:27:53.376Z","harness:codex","CLI subprocess acceptance and direct SDK persistence tests prove different risks: bundled child execution does not instrument the source owner. Source coverage exposed full-depth read rejection and unexercised multi-candidate ranking; meaningful round-trip and ordering cases now cover those contracts before closure."
